Author: JBKingdon <james.kingdon@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Mar 22 08:03:49 2020 -0400

    Optimise hop sequence randomisation
    
    The existing sequence randomisation code relies on a random search
    of the channel space to find a suitable next channel. As the number of
    possible channels increases this gets increasingly slow, as the
    probability of finding a suitable channel becomes lower.
    
    The new algorithm uses an array of flags to track suitable channels
    remaining at each step and is therefore much quicker to find a
    suitable channel. This provides noticeably quicker rx startup with
    20 channels and much quicker startup with 40.
    
    This PR also introduces Regulatory_Domain_FCC_915 with an extended
    FHSSfreqs array.
    
    Signed-off-by: JBKingdon <james.kingdon@gmail.com>

